From fbaa875bbe04e1e0503b850c9074e23ac59235fd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Z User <z@container>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 19:11:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 15/16] phase3: state-hash ranged terms + pool block + the
 pool's subsystem home

- BattleStateHash.cpp: block 8 (per-entity ranged terms appended AFTER the
  charge block, same sorted-handle pass, zero-fill when the fragment is
  absent: AmmoCount, ReloadTimer 1e-2, ShotsFired -- spawn-immutable fields
  excluded per the base-stats precedent) + block 9 (the projectile pool:
  live count + per-live-entry Pos/Vel/TTL at 1e-2 in INDEX order, RC8).
- BattleProjectileSubsystem.h/.cpp (new): the pool's game-thread lifetime
  owner (ReserveForBattle reads the PoolCapacity cvar once per battle;
  ResetForBattle clears) -- ships with the data spine so the hash's pool
  block has its read surface from day one; the fire/step processors remain
  the pipeline task's work. FBattleProjectilePool::EmptyPool() is the
  null-subsystem fold (zero-capacity static).
- MassBattleCombatTests HashTerms extended: ranged-row spawn (Peasant
  Archers), ammo/reload/shots mutation sensitivity with reverts, pool
  acquire/mutate/release hash sensitivity (spec section 3.4).

MUST re-run on the UE machine: unit tier (HashTerms + the ranged suite
green; melee-only hashes unchanged by construction -- the zero-fill term
count is fixed). Static patch: brace-balanced, include-complete; no engine
build was available at author time.
